              "name": "How often should I actually come in for a cleaning?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "It depends on your bacterial risk and gum health, not a universal schedule. Some patients do well with twice-yearly visits. Others with active gum disease or high bacterial loads benefit from every three or four months. We determine your recall frequency based on your data."
