              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "My gums bleed when I brush. Is that normal?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Bleeding gums are one of the earliest signs of bacterial infection in the gum tissue. It is common but not normal, and it is not fixed by brushing harder. It is a signal that the bacterial environment around your gums needs attention."
